# Customer APP — Canonical Navigation & Core Menu Capability Contract

Task lineage:
- `AIPIFY.CUSTOMER.APP.CANONICAL.NAV.AND.CATALOG.FOUNDATION.V1`
- `AIPIFY.CORE.CANONICAL.APP.MENU.CAPABILITY.CONTRACT.V1`

## Ownership

| Concern | Owner |
|---|---|
| Capability ids, entitlements, role/permission, readiness, visibility, reason codes | **Core** (`lib/core/app-menu-capability/`) |
| Group order, locale labels, icons, active route, responsive layout | **APP** (`APP_PORTAL_NAV_GROUPS`) |
| Product/package catalog, commercial grant/revoke initiation | **Platform** |

## Absolute rules

1. **Core owns APP capability visibility.** APP never decides entitlement, role, readiness, or foundation visibility.
2. **`APP_PORTAL_NAV_GROUPS` is presentation only** — maps Core-allowed ids to labels, icons, routes, groups.
3. **No dynamic item after Core filter.** Dynamic navigation may contribute suspension notices only — never append menu items after Core resolution.
4. **No mega-nav fallback.** `lib/app/nav-config.ts` must not drive Customer APP menu rendering and must not grow as a parallel register.
5. **Unknown capability ids fail closed** — hidden, never rendered, never treated as allowed.
6. **Foundation always hidden** — never restored from dynamic payload, stale cache, or fallback mega-nav.
7. **Available / pending are catalog-only** — not operative main-menu items before activation.
8. **Entitlement revoke removes nav** on the next Core bundle (org/user/version keyed; layout is force-dynamic).
9. **Server route authorization remains mandatory** — menu hiding is not access control.
10. Products without entitlement appear in **`/app/software`**, not as half-finished main-menu items.
11. **`/app/settings` requires server-side owner/admin** via `requireAppSettingsOwnerAdminAccess` — direct URL must not rely on nav hiding alone.

## Canonical resolution order

1. Core resolves organization + user (trusted session)
2. Core resolves role / permissions
3. Core resolves package / modules / packs / licenses
4. Core resolves readiness
5. Core returns allowed capability ids + states
6. APP maps ids → presentation metadata
7. APP renders only allowed ids

## Fail-closed

On resolver/load failure: minimal safe operational nav from Core (`buildFailClosedAppMenuCapabilityBundle`). Never full mega-nav. Never unfiltered dynamic payload. Never foundation.

